# Unity rebuild architecture

Read `Docs/UNITY_REQUIREMENTS.md`.

- Use Unity 6 and frozen package versions.
- UI Toolkit for application scenes and complex/data-heavy gameplay panels.
- uGUI screen-space Canvas for gameplay HUD/feedback.
- uGUI world-space Canvas for in-world markers and prompts.
- One mission scene with three logical open-world areas.
- No one-scene-per-area architecture.
- No additive area loading.
- No separate final-challenge scene/state; Area 3 includes it.
- Keep static gameplay content local.
- Keep Quiz Portal server-managed.
- Use stable IDs and the canonical v5 manifest and per-mission JSON catalog.
- Use local-first transactional progress plus outbox.
- Do not edit vendor packages.
- Avoid cyclic assemblies and runtime object-name searches.
- Add validation and tests.
